# 6. PHOTO STORAGE AND PRIVACY

Photos must NEVER be stored in a publicly accessible bucket.

Use:

```text
Private Storage
       ↓
Backend authorization
       ↓
Temporary signed URL
       ↓
Frontend
```

The frontend must never receive permanent public image URLs.

When a user requests a photo:

1. Authenticate the user.
2. Verify group membership.
3. Verify that the user has permission to view the photo.
4. Generate a short-lived signed URL.
5. Return the URL to the frontend.
6. URL expires after a configurable period.

Use configurable values such as:

```text
SIGNED_URL_EXPIRATION_SECONDS=300
```

Do not hard-code this.

