# 63. FINAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The application is considered functionally complete for MVP when:

### Authentication

* A user can create an account.
* A user can log in/out.
* A user can edit their profile.

### Groups

* A user can create a group.
* A user can join using an invite.
* A group can have admins and members.
* Admins can remove members.

### Photos

* A member can upload one photo per day.
* Duplicate daily posts are prevented server-side.
* Images are stored privately.
* Images are served using temporary signed URLs.
* EXIF/GPS metadata is stripped.
* Users can delete their own photos.

### Feed

* Members can see authorized classmates' photos.
* Users can react.
* Users can report inappropriate content.

### Memories

* Users can browse previous days.
* Users can browse a calendar.
* Users can view their own photo history.

### Notifications

* Users can receive daily reminders.
* Notification preferences can be changed.

### Safety

* Non-members cannot access group photos.
* Users cannot modify other users' posts.
* Users can report content.
* Admins can moderate content.
* Account deletion works.

### Architecture

* Frontend and backend are completely separated.
* Database is separately organized.
* Storage provider is abstracted.
* UI components are reusable.
* Theme is centralized.
* API is documented.
* Environment variables are documented.
* Critical business rules have automated tests.

