# 64. IMPORTANT FINAL INSTRUCTION TO THE AI CODING AGENT

Do not simply generate a visual prototype.

Build the application as a real, maintainable product with:

```text
Frontend
+
Backend
+
Database
+
Private Object Storage
+
Authentication
+
Authorization
+
Notifications
+
Moderation
+
Testing
+
Documentation
```

Prioritize the daily photo loop first.

Every architectural decision must preserve the ability to completely redesign the frontend later.

The frontend is a replaceable layer.

The backend/API and database should remain stable even if the entire visual design is replaced.

Build the system so that another developer can open the repository six months later, understand the architecture quickly, replace the UI, add a feature, change the storage provider, or modify the database without having to reverse-engineer a tangled codebase.

Start with a working MVP, but structure the codebase so all advanced features listed above can be added incrementally without architectural rewrites.
